# Project Core Rules

CSCI 544 project: two separate experiments, static trust and dynamic trust, continue the same CGA-WIKI openings with personas A and B. A blind judge marks each conversation 0 or 1, which is compared with the real personal-attack label. `docs/DECISIONS.md` section G records the agreed design; `README.md` describes the pipeline.

## Information flow (never violate)

- Only the comparison step (`evaluate_run` in `src/trustsim/pipeline.py` and `src/trustsim/evaluation/`) reads real labels. Simulation and judging receive `Seed` objects, never `Example` or `Label`.
- Agents and the critic see only the conversation so far: never labels, later human turns, or which experiment they are in. Agents are not shown their trust value; the critic never sees trust.
- Judge input is the conversation text with speakers renamed Editor 1 and Editor 2, plus the fixed prompt. No experiment name, trust, persona, model id, or label.
- Static and dynamic share openings, personas, starting trust, models, prompts, turn limit, and judge. Only whether trust moves differs.

## Where things live

- Shared types: `trustsim.dialogue` (`Turn`, `Seed`) and `trustsim.data.loader` (`Label`, `Example`). Do not redefine them.
- One folder per pipeline stage under `src/trustsim/`: `data`, `personas`, `simulation`, `judge`, `evaluation`, plus `llm` for model access.
- Tunable values go in `configs/*.yaml`, prompt text in `prompts/*_vN.txt`. No hardcoded prompts or magic numbers in code.
- Entry points live in `scripts/`; package modules do not run anything on import.

## Safety and reproducibility

- Never commit or log API keys; read them from environment variables.
- Never commit `data/raw/`, `data/processed/`, or `outputs/`.
- A failed conversation is saved with its status and error and retried on the next run; never drop it silently.
- Each run's `run.json` records settings, prompt hashes, git commit, and token usage. A run folder cannot be resumed with different settings.
- Pin new dependencies as `name==version` in `requirements.txt` and `pyproject.toml`. Target Python 3.12+.
